app orb-release-spec [
  version: "1.0.0",
  inbound: ["cli-release"],
  description: "Design contract for `orb release [--publish] [--major|--minor|--patch] [--language-major] [--severity security|critical|normal --advisory <text> --fixes <range>]`: the release publisher for the packages in release.json. Without --publish it reads each entry's version, computes the next with std-semver and prints the plan, writing nothing. With --publish, per entry in order: the version and the dependents' ranges are written, then git add, commit, tag, push of main and the tag, and a registry poll until the version is listed; a released entry is skipped so a re-run resumes. Every package.json it writes also gets a top-level orbRelease block in the same write as the new version: severity (default normal), plus advisory and fixes (a semver range of the package's earlier versions it fixes) for security and critical only; a Cargo.toml entry gets none, and the plan shows the block. A package.json that declares orbLanguage { version, sources } is the language data owner (@almadar/core): sources lists the repo-relative files and directories that produce the language data it ships, and a release without it stops the run naming orbLanguage.sources. When a path in sources changed since the entry's last tag, the release raises orbLanguage.version in the same write as the new version, a minor bump by default or a major bump with --language-major (the orb kernel must then be changed to read the new major, and the plan says so in a warning line); the plan shows `language <old> -> <new>` on the row. --language-major is refused before any write when no released entry's language data changed. Security or critical without both advisory and fixes, normal with either, or an unknown severity is refused before anything is written. Extra arguments or two bump flags answer the usage (status 400, exit 2); a stopped run answers status 500."
]

orbital OrbReleaseSpec {
  expects trait OrbRelease {
    state ready
    state parsing
    state running
    emits {
      RELEASE_ANSWERED { status : number!  body : string!  stderr : string }
    }
  }
  expects page boot -> OrbRelease
}
